    "lawCode": "Amd Title, §§2, 3 & 4, Chap of 2020 (as proposed in S.8417 & A.10492); amd §91, Pub Serv L; amd §5, Chap of 2020 (as proposed in S.8113-A & A.10521); amd §9-x, Bank L (as proposed in S.8243-C & A.10351-B); amd §180.65, CP L (as proposed in S.8414 & A.10493)",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8428\n\nSPONSOR: PARKER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend a chapter of the laws of 2020 amending the local finance\nlaw relating to bond anticipation notes issued in calendar years 2015\nthrough 2021, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S. 8417 and A.\n10492, in relation to expenditures and temporary transfer of reserve\nfunds for expenses related to state disaster emergency declared pursuant\nto executive order 202 of 2020 and authorizing the extension of repay-\nment of inter-fund advances made for expenses related to state disaster\nemergency declared pursuant to executive order 202 of 2020 (Part A); to\namend the public service law, in relation to issuing a moratorium on\nutility termination of services during periods of pandemics and/or state\nof emergencies; and to amend a chapter of the laws of 2020 amending the\npublic service law, relating to issuing a moratorium on utility termi-\nnation of services during periods of pandemics and/or state of emergen-\ncies, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S.8113-A and A.10521, in\nrelation to the effectiveness thereof (Part B); to amend the banking\nlaw, in relation to the forbearance of residential mortgage payments\n(Part C); and to amend the criminal procedure law, in relation to hear-\nings conducted on a felony complaint during a state disaster emergency\n(Part D)\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to make technical changes to chapters of the\nlaws of 2020, legislative bill numbers A.10492 and 5.8417 (Part A);\nlegislative bills numbers S.8113-A and A.10521\n\n(Part B); legislative bill numbers A.10351-B and S.8243-C (Part C); and\nlegislative bill numbers A.10493 and S.8414 (Part D)\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nPart A makes technical chapter amendments to A.10492 and S.8417.\n\nSection 1. Makes technical changes of the title of a chapter of the laws\nof 2020, Assembly bill number A. 10492 and Senate bill number S.8417.\n\nSection 2. Makes technical changes to clarify that the period described\nin the bill as the \"COVID-19 pandemic\" refers to the State disaster\nemergency declared by Executive Order 202 of 2020.\n\nSection 3. Requires that the temporary transfer of funds by munici-\npalities or special districts, including fire districts and school\ndistricts be used to pay for operating or other costs attributable to\nthe State disaster emergency declaration related to COVID-19.\n\nSection 4. Makes technical changes to clarify that the \"COVID-19 pandem-\nic\" refers to the COVID-19 State disaster emergency declaration.  Part B\nmakes technical chapter amendments to S.8113-A and A.10521\n\nSection 1. Amends subdivisions 9, 10 and 12 of § 91 of the Public\nService law, as added by a chapter of the laws of 2020, to: 1) allow\nduring the COVID-19 state of emergency, telephone corporations to not\nreconnect service if such service was disconnected due to reasons other\nthan non-payment of a charge by a customer, and disconnect service at\nthe request of the customer; and, 2) require that telephone corporations\nnot terminate service to customers who defaulted on deferred payment\nagreement or owe arrears to the company for a period of 180 days after\nthe state of emergency is lifted, when such customer has experienced a\nchange in financial circumstances due to the emergency.\n\nSection 2. Adds an expiration clause to the chapter, of March 31, 2021.\nPart C makes technical chapter amendments to A.10351-B and S.8243-C\nAmends the underlying chapter by adding new language to allow mortgage\nservicers and state-chartered banks to refrain from giving forbearance\nrelief if the servicer or bank has liquidity or soundness issues. If a\nbank or servicer declines to give forbearance for such reasons, the bank\nor servicer must notify the Department of Financial Services within five\ndays to provide details regarding such. This new language also clarifies\nthat any financial hardship justifying forbearance must be related to\nthe COVID19 crisis. Further, the language clarifies that mortgage\nforbearance must be given for the full monthly payment (which would\ninclude taxes and insurance, for many mortgagors). In addition, the new\nlanguage exempts SONYMA (State of New York Mortgage Authority) from the\nprovisions of the legislation.\n\nPart D makes technical chapter amendments to A.10493 and 5.8414 Amends\nthe underlying legislation which authorizes the audio-visual appearance\nof any party or witness at such a hearing, held pursuant to Article 180\nof the Criminal Procedure Law, where the court finds that due to the\nperson's circumstances and such disaster emergency a personal appearance\nby such party or witness would be an unreasonable hardship to such\nperson or witness. The parties need only to communicate such hardship to\nthe Court for this finding to be made.  This bill does not require a\nseparate hearing to determine if an unreasonable hardship exists.\n\nSection 1. Adds additional phrases to confirm that the request for audi-\no-visual proceedings of this type may be made on motion of the parties,\na witness or the court, that among the factors to be considered is\nwhether personal appearance would create an unreasonable health risk to\nthe public, court staff or any other person involved in the proceeding,\nand that a copy of any recorded appearance shall be provided to the\nparties\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill makes necessary technical changes to provisions relating to\nthe COVID-19 state disaster emergency\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately, provided, however, that the\napplicable effective date of Parts A though D of this act shall be as\nspecifically set forth in the last section of such Parts.\n",
